# AoC 2022 Day 8 — Grid demonstrator.
#
# Parses the tree-height grid into a Grid<Int> and counts the "tall" trees
# (height >= 5). For the example grid that is 9.
#
# NOTE: the full Part 1 visibility solve (count trees visible from outside)
# needs per-cell line-of-sight reductions over rows/columns, which require
# expression-layer list operations deferred past v0.2 (same blocker as Day 5).
# This program exercises grid construction + a cell predicate end-to-end.
Cursed Energy: input.txt
Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
Cursed Technique: Split Each by ""
Channeled Energy: Convert Each List to Integers
Channeled Energy: Convert To Grid
Maximum Technique: Count Cells
    Using: (h) -> h >= 5
Reveal: stdout
